      <h2 id="scs-title" class="mt-5 max-w-3xl font-display text-3xl font-medium tracking-[-0.05em] md:text-4xl">Sovereignty is a control surface, not a region label.</h2>
      <p id="scs-caption" class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">The same data product may cross clouds, jurisdictions, and service boundaries. This surface makes locality, portability, and control explicit before the platform is selected.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="scs-code" aria-hidden="true">CLOUD / DATA<br /><span>CONTROL SURFACE</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="scs-surface" role="img" aria-label="Three horizontal control bands connect data locality, workload portability, and operating controls across a multicloud estate." tabindex="0">
    <div class="scs-provider-rail"><span>Workload context</span><span>Data product</span><span>Decision owner</span></div>
    <div class="scs-band is-locality"><strong>Locality</strong><span>Where data is stored, processed, backed up, and inspected.</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i><b>jurisdiction · residency · purpose</b></div>
    <div class="scs-band is-portability"><strong>Portability</strong><span>How a service can move or degrade without losing its contract.</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i><b>interfaces · exit path · recovery</b></div>
    <div class="scs-band is-control"><strong>Control</strong><span>Who can access, change, price, and stop the system.</span><i aria-hidden="true"></i><b>identity · evidence · cost</b></div>
  </div>

  <div class="scs-table-wrap" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable cloud and data control questions" tabindex="0">
    <table>
      <caption>Questions to resolve before committing a cloud or data workload</caption>
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Surface</th><th scope="col">Decision question</th><th scope="col">Useful artifact</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Locality</th><td>What must remain in a jurisdiction, and for which purpose?</td><td>Data classification and residency register</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Portability</th><td>What is the viable exit, failover, or service degradation path?</td><td>Dependency map and recovery test</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Control</th><td>Which role approves access, spend, change, and shutdown?</td><td>Control matrix with evidence owner</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="scs-footer">
    <p id="scs-note"><strong>Reading note:</strong> provider choice is downstream of the control surface. The diagram is an operating prompt, not a cloud-provider comparison or a claim of residency by itself.</p>
